<section class="hero"><div class="hero-inner"><span class="hero-tag">North Carolina</span><h1>NC Labor Laws</h1><p>Worker protections, regulations, and compliance requirements under North Carolina state law.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-inner"><div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Topic</th><th>Summary</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>1</td><td>Minimum Wage</td><td>NC follows federal minimum wage ($7.25/hr). No separate state minimum above federal.</td></tr>
<tr><td>2</td><td>Overtime</td><td>Time-and-a-half for hours exceeding 40/week under FLSA. No state-specific overtime law.</td></tr>
<tr><td>3</td><td>Break Requirements</td><td>No NC law requires meal/rest breaks for adults. Minors under 16: 30-min break after 5 hours.</td></tr>
<tr><td>4</td><td>Discrimination</td><td>NC Equal Employment Practices Act prohibits discrimination based on race, religion, color, national origin, age, sex, disability.</td></tr>
<tr><td>5</td><td>Workplace Safety</td><td>NC OSH Act — state-run OSHA program. Employers must provide safe working conditions.</td></tr>
<tr><td>6</td><td>Workers Compensation</td><td>NC Workers' Compensation Act. Employers with 3+ employees must carry insurance.</td></tr>
<tr><td>7</td><td>Unemployment Insurance</td><td>Division of Employment Security administers UI benefits. Max 12–20 weeks depending on state rate.</td></tr>
<tr><td>8</td><td>Child Labor Laws</td><td>Youth Employment Certificate required for minors. Restricted hours for under-16. Prohibited hazardous occupations.</td></tr>
<tr><td>9</td><td>At-Will Employment</td><td>NC is an at-will state. Either party can terminate employment at any time for any lawful reason.</td></tr>
<tr><td>10</td><td>OSHA Compliance</td><td>NC DOL enforces workplace safety standards. Inspections, citations, penalties for violations.</td></tr>
<tr><td>11</td><td>Wage Payment</td><td>NC Wage and Hour Act — employers must pay agreed wages on regular paydays. Final pay within 24 hours of demand.</td></tr>
<tr><td>12</td><td>Retaliatory Employment Discrimination</td><td>REDA protects employees who file workers' comp claims, report safety violations, or engage in protected activity.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></div></section>
